Subject: control mode, start at a given time, and say when the file will end

To play files one after the other with no gap, the program of the next file waits,
paused, and starts at the exact time the one before it ends.

  end T          said once, when the disk thread has read the whole file: T is the
                 frame time of JACK (jack_last_frame_time, which wraps) at which the
                 last frame of the file will have been played, at the rate of the
                 server
  play at T      play, from the beginning of the cycle in which time T comes, with
                 silence before T inside that cycle; if T has passed, play now

A start at a given time fades in over 32 frames only, not over a cycle, because
the file goes on from the end of the one before. pause and seek cancel a start
that has not come. The announcement is said again after a pause or a seek, as the
time of the end has changed. It is not said with -l.

Measured on a dummy server with a file at 44.1 kHz and the next one at 48 kHz, for
periods of 512 to 2048 frames and for 44.1, 48 and 96 kHz: no frame of silence
between the two (before, up to one period, 5 to 20 ms depending on the length
of the file), and no overlap.
